cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CBR-RD-Agent, please cite the paper below."
title: "CBR-Enhanced RD-Agent for Kaggle Data Science"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Stocker
    given-names: Felix
    email: felix.stocker@sto-eng.de
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-25"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/stofe94/cbr-rd-agent"
abstract: >-
  CBR-RD-Agent extends Microsoft's RD-Agent, reduced to its data science scenario,
  with Case-Based Reasoning: successful experiments are stored as structured cases
  and retrieved at proposal and coding time, failures are tracked, and a five-gate
  quality pipeline decides what is retained. A Google AI Studio backend runs
  Gemma 4 as the reasoning model.
keywords:
  - case-based reasoning
  - LLM agents
  - autonomous data science
  - Kaggle
  - MLE-bench
  - RD-Agent
